{{- define "resolved-reference-context" -}}
{{- if ne .ResolvedReferenceContext ""}}

=== RESOLVED REFERENCE CONTEXT ===
The compositor resolved the strict carrier content and its declared direct
references at integration HEAD before launch. Treat this bounded context as
inherited authority. Do not re-read or replace its pinned source paths with worktree content.
A reference marked "section changed since its pinned revision" or "no longer
resolves" drifted after its carrier was approved: that approval did not cover the
text shown, so if the difference bears on your task, raise it rather than rely on it silently.
A reference marked "not inlined" was declared by an ancestor carrier, and a
section marked "peer of your assigned section" belongs to a sibling task of an
artifact you were assigned one section of; read either with the git show command
on its line only if your task needs it.
Read outside it only for evidence owned by your stage or an unresolved dependency
that the assigned context identifies.

{{.ResolvedReferenceContext}}
{{- if .LegacyArtifactReferences}}

=== LEGACY ARTIFACT REFERENCES ===
These task refs were not strict carriers at integration HEAD and retain the legacy read path:
{{- range .LegacyArtifactReferences}}
- {{.Field}} {{.Ref}}: read {{$.Worktree}}/{{.File}} first; if absent, use `git -C {{$.Worktree}} show {{$.IntegrationBranch}}:{{.File}}`.
{{- end}}
{{- end}}
